 "title": "Where the Library Ends",
 "subtitle": "Shelves of scent in basalt, Jeju",
 "line": "At the end of a library the books run out, and the shelves keep going with scent.",
 "synopsis": "You walk out of the last aisle of a library into a room lined with the same shelves, but every slot holds an amber bottle instead of a book. The walls are layered clay like the cut of a Jeju cliff, and the floor is dark basalt that still smells of rain on stone. In the centre, under a low plaster dome, a round basalt basin runs with water, and you stop to wash your hands before you read anything. Two long reading tables hold open testers like open pages, and the counter waits quietly at the back.",
